Subject: META: Adjudication Decision on Mr. Singh's request

This is my decision concerning Pandit Singh's request for adjudication
concerning the result of his complaint against Perry Metzger.  I'm
hoping that by posting my decisions, the list rules will be generally
clearer.  This is part of the reason for such a long post.  

If you have any questions or comments, please feel free to email me
at andreag@csmil.umich.edu

Andrea Gallagher
Adjudicator

---------------------------------------------------------------------

Mr. Singh,

You requested that your "sentence" from the List Administrator
be reduced for a number of reasons.  Both the original judgement
against you, and your objections to that judgement are included
below.

I have examined the judgement, and will reduce the punishment, but
generally not for the reasons that you objected.  My responses to
your objections are at the end of this message.

Mr. Shapiro identified two violations of the list rules.

1) not using the Meta: prefix in requesting judgment

For this violation he gave you one warning, out of 3 before
you can be removed from the list for a period of time.

I think this is reasonable and a good use of the warning.  
Essentially, you are being told that this behavior does
violate the list rules but that none of your list 
privilages will be revoked unless you do this repeatedly.

2) sending the request for judgment to the list as a whole,
   instead of sending it to the list administration

You were given 2 warnings for this.  I am reducing that to
1 warning.

Though posting your complaint publicly looks more formal than
starting a fight on the list, it has much the same flavor.  This
is one of the most serious rules that we have on this list.

However, the argument that Mr. Shapiro used in addressing this
point seemed to have more to do with the type of posts you had
been making in general, and little to do with the no-fighting
rule.  It seems as if he was addressing the additional warning
to the posts about flying yogis.  While I think the list needs
to deal with polite posts that most members see as noise and
not signal, I don't think it should be arbitrarily punished
under the guise of current rules.

In addition, Mr. Shapiro requested that you use prefixes on all
your posts, not just those relating to meta-topics such as list
administration.  I don't see any authority behind this request,
since he did not say that it was a warning.  But because it
came from the List Administrator, it clearly sounded like a
command.

I am overturning that request, and you should not think that it carries
any weight.  At the moment the use of prefixes is etiquette, though
very important etiquette.  The only prefixes that are required are
Meta, Pledge, and Poll; because these can be high-traffic with
no interest to many members.  I do not like the idea of certain
list members being required to use prefixes that others use
optionally.

In summary, you have been given two warnings.  After you have been
given three warnings, the List Administrator has evidence that you
consistently violate rules, out of bad faith rather than ignorance.
At that point your list privileges could be suspended or canceled
for any further complaints.

I hope this is satisfactory.  If you have any objections that might
sway my decision, you can reply before tomorrow at 4:00 EST when
I post this decision to the list.



