Subject: EXT: Kids vs. Uploading

	I greatly dislike the concept of having children as form of life
extension. Being a dependent child myself (not for long! :-),
independent of mind and spirit, I am offended when my parents try to
live through me. (I posted a bit about this before.) While a case might
be made that they have some sort of "right" to do this, given that they
have fed, clothed, and housed me for the past 18 years, I am an
individual and I am not an "extension" of my parents, even though my
genes are completely from my father & mother. (No recombination done
when I was conceived...)
	I think a fundamental difference between a future-me being
extremely different from the now-me and the parent-child situation is
that I am alive *and* my parents are alive at this time. Although my
future-me could be completely different from the now-me and share the
same genetics, there would be no conflict because the now-me would not
be alive, while now, both my parents and I are alive.

